      "worked": "In $(1+x)^n(1+x)^n$, the terms producing $x^n$ are obtained by multiplying $\\binom{n}{k}x^k$ from the first factor by $\\binom{n}{n-k}x^{n-k}$ from the second, for $k=0,1,\\ldots,n$.\n\nThe coefficient of $x^n$ in $(1+x)^{2n}$ is $\\binom{2n}{n}$. Equating coefficients and using $\\binom{n}{n-k}=\\binom{n}{k}$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{2n}{n}&=\\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\binom{n}{k}\\binom{n}{n-k}\\\\\\binom{2n}{n}&=\\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\binom{n}{k}^{2}\\\\\\binom{2n}{n}&=\\binom{n}{0}^{2}+\\binom{n}{1}^{2}+\\cdots+\\binom{n}{n}^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
